 faq=[('h3','[H2] Frequently Asked Questions'),
  ('p','**Is the Evac+Chair 600H an evacuation wheelchair?**'),
  ('p','It does the job of an evacuation wheelchair on the stairs. It is a folding evacuation chair, not an everyday wheelchair: the passenger moves into the chair, and the operator guides it down the stairs on its tracks.'),
  ('p','**Can the 600H go up the stairs?**'),
  ('p','Yes, with help. One operator takes the 600H down the stairs. For upward evacuation, 2 to 4 people use the fold-away front and rear grab handles to lift the chair up the stairs.'),
  ('p','**What is the dual-position seat?**'),
  ('p','The seat can be used flat, with zipped side panels, or as a hammock seat by releasing the side panels and fastening them underneath. The over-thigh quick-release restraint works in both positions.'),
  ('p','**How is the 600H different from the 300H?**'),
  ('p','The 600H adds fold-away front and rear grab handles, so 2 to 4 people can carry it up the stairs or through difficult access. The 300H is the lighter standard model for downward evacuation.')],
